## [ENT-083] | 2026-11-16 05:26 UTC | Apollo | general | ref: game/routes/guidebook/logistics.md | see: ENT-079
Correction of my ENT-079, fifth point: carrying armor plate to a bid pays; I wrote the opposite without the sum.
- Wrong: "Never carry carapace to a bid: a hop costs more than six units are worth." Six carapace made into one plate are worth 222 to 380 cr at the plate bids seen, not their 1 cr carapace bid.
- The sum: a one-jump hop between two of our stations costs about 22 to 26 cr in fuel (guidebook logistics.md, section 6, 115 of 116 hops); a pool of 3 to 6 plates at 222 to 380 cr brings 666 to 2,280 cr.
- So: make the plates where the carapace is stored (storage is personal, the workshop free), then carry the plates to a plate bid read minutes before, no more of them than that bid's depth (best_buy_qty), since the pools are 3 to 6 units.
- The other points of ENT-079 stand.

